<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Kumu

//kumu// — Hawaiian: teacher, origin, source, trunk; the base from which things grow. In botany,
the trunk of a tree; in cultural life, the teacher who holds the root knowledge and passes it
forward. A kumu functions as more than a fact-holder — it grounds the structural origin of a lineage of forms.

A kumu names a template of a Verse-style messaging edge widget set — a `creative_device`-shaped
device definition, carrying `@editable` slots and reaction pins for `kau` to place. The
definition teaches; the placement creates
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kau#/etymology`).

Where `wehe` / `\procedure` declares a named callable body, `kumu` declares a named
//device type// — a reusable widget-set shape that `kau` instances stand up on the island map.
The distinction: a procedure executes; a kumu holds the form other nodes instantiate.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/device-model>>

!! The Device Model

A kumu declaration carries three parts, mapped from the Verse `creative_device` model
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kumu-device#/verse-model`):

* ''`@editable` slots'' — properties the declaration exposes as ahu slot URIs; `kau` supplies
  the value at placement time (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kau#/law`).
* ''OUTPUT pins, `KumuListenable`'' — the device's outgoing events, carried as
  `reaction:listenable` pranala edges on the type meme.
* ''INPUT pins, `KumuSubscribable`'' — the device's handler surface, carried as
  `reaction:subscribable` pranala edges on the type meme.

Wiring between two kau instances' pins runs through `papalohe`
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/papalohe`); a kumu declaration never wires directly to another
kumu declaration — only placed instances wire.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Law (Kānāwai)

A kumu declaration MUST carry a unique type name.
A kumu declaration body defines the widget-set template for instances of that type.
A kumu declaration MUST register a type definition only, producing no render output.
A kumu declaration's `@editable` slots MUST resolve as ahu slot URIs.
A kumu declaration's OUTPUT/INPUT pins derive from the type meme's `reaction:listenable` /
`reaction:subscribable` pranala edges, not a TS class hierarchy
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kumu-device#/exports`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/syntax>>

!! Syntax

```text
<<~ kumu TypeName(params)>>
  body template
<<~/kumu>>
```

The TW5 `\type` and `\typos` pragmas run as native TW5 pragmas in their own right, carrying no
Hawaiian headword and no mirror relation to `kumu`
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nihomano-sigils#/first-discovered-set`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pending>>

!! Pending

A `kahea` name-form call resolves a kumu type at widget-build time through the `KumuRegistry`
into a `WidgetNode`; the registry's own resolution step stays open, held at Gap 8 of the
research stream <confidence:0.6 — design resolved, implementation pending>
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/research-streams/gaps-tensions#/gaps`).

<<~/ahu>>

